sequenceDiagram
    title Insurance Business Process Sequence Diagram<br/>Quotation → Policy Issuance → Payment → Cancellation

    autonumber

    actor Customer
    participant Agent
    participant Provider as Insurance Provider
    participant Underwriting as Underwriting Team
    participant PaymentProcessor as Payment Processor
    participant Operations as Operations Team
    participant System as Insurance Core System

    %% 1. Quotation Creation
    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over Customer,System: 1. Quotation Creation

    Customer->>Agent: Request vehicle insurance quotation
    Agent->>Customer: Collect customer and vehicle information

    Agent->>System: Create Customer / Vehicle records if not existing
    System-->>Agent: Customer and Vehicle records available

    Agent->>System: Create Quotation<br/>Status = QUOTED
    System-->>Agent: Quotation created

    Agent->>System: Add Quotation Item(s)<br/>Coverage, sum insured, deductible
    System-->>Agent: Quotation Item(s) saved

    System->>Provider: Submit quotation information
    Provider->>Underwriting: Request underwriting review if required

    alt Underwriting approval required
        Underwriting->>Underwriting: Review customer, vehicle, coverage, premium
        Underwriting-->>Provider: Approve / reject quotation
    else No underwriting approval required
        Provider->>Provider: Apply standard pricing and eligibility rules
    end

    Provider-->>System: Return quotation decision and premium
    System-->>Agent: Quotation ready for customer review
    Agent->>Customer: Present quotation details<br/>Premium, coverage, expiry date
    end

    %% 2. Quotation Decision
    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over Customer,System: 2. Quotation Decision

    alt Customer accepts quotation before expiry
        Customer->>Agent: Accept quotation
        Agent->>System: Update Quotation<br/>Status = ACCEPTED
        System-->>Agent: Quotation accepted

        System->>System: Convert accepted quotation to policy
        System->>System: Update Quotation<br/>Status = CONVERTED

        %% 3. Policy Issuance
        Note over System,Provider: 3. Policy Issuance

        System->>Provider: Request policy issuance
        Provider->>System: Issue policy<br/>Policy Status = ISSUED
        System-->>Agent: Policy issued

        Note right of System: Business meaning:<br/>- QUOTED = quotation has been generated and is ready for customer review<br/>- ACCEPTED = customer agrees with quotation<br/>- CONVERTED = quotation has been used to create policy<br/>- ISSUED = policy has been generated<br/>- ACTIVE may depend on start date and/or successful payment

        %% 4. Payment Creation and Processing
        Note over Customer,System: 4. Payment Creation and Processing

        System->>PaymentProcessor: Create payment request<br/>Payment Status = PENDING
        PaymentProcessor-->>Agent: Send payment instruction / payment link
        Agent-->>Customer: Forward payment instruction / payment link

        Customer->>PaymentProcessor: Make premium payment

        alt Payment successful
            PaymentProcessor->>System: Confirm payment<br/>Payment Status = PAID
            System->>System: Check policy start date and activation rules

            alt Policy start date reached and activation conditions met
                System->>System: Update Policy<br/>Status = ACTIVE
                System-->>Agent: Policy activated
                Agent-->>Customer: Confirm active policy
            else Policy start date is in the future
                System->>System: Keep Policy Status = ISSUED<br/>Activate on start date
                System-->>Agent: Policy issued, pending activation date
                Agent-->>Customer: Confirm policy issued
            end

        else Payment failed
            PaymentProcessor->>System: Payment failed<br/>Payment Status = FAILED
            System-->>Operations: Notify failed payment case
            Operations->>Agent: Request payment follow-up with customer
            Agent->>Customer: Follow up for retry payment

            alt Customer retries payment successfully
                Customer->>PaymentProcessor: Retry payment
                PaymentProcessor->>System: Confirm payment<br/>Payment Status = PAID
                System->>System: Check policy start date and activation rules

                alt Policy start date reached and activation conditions met
                    System->>System: Update Policy<br/>Status = ACTIVE
                    System-->>Agent: Policy activated after retry
                    Agent-->>Customer: Confirm active policy
                else Policy start date is in the future
                    System->>System: Keep Policy Status = ISSUED<br/>Activate on start date
                    System-->>Agent: Policy issued, pending activation date
                    Agent-->>Customer: Confirm policy issued
                end

            else Payment remains unpaid after grace period
                Operations->>System: Mark overdue / unpaid case
                System->>System: Apply business rule<br/>Policy may remain ISSUED, become CANCELLED, or EXPIRED
                System-->>Agent: Notify unpaid policy outcome
                Agent-->>Customer: Inform unpaid policy outcome
            end
        end

    else Customer rejects quotation
        Customer->>Agent: Reject quotation
        Agent->>System: Update Quotation<br/>Status = REJECTED
        System-->>Agent: Quotation rejected

        Note right of System: No policy should be created<br/>No payment should be required

    else Quotation expires before customer decision
        System->>System: Check quotation expiry date
        System->>System: Update Quotation<br/>Status = EXPIRED
        System-->>Agent: Quotation expired
        Agent-->>Customer: Inform quotation expired

        Note right of System: Expired quotations are not converted to policy.<br/>A new quotation or re-quotation may be required based on business rules.
    end
    end

    %% 5. Cancellation Lifecycle
    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over Customer,System: 5. Cancellation Lifecycle

    opt Customer requests policy cancellation
        Customer->>Agent: Request policy cancellation
        Agent->>System: Submit cancellation request

        System->>Operations: Validate cancellation eligibility
        Operations->>System: Review policy status, effective date, payment, refund rule

        alt Cancellation approved
            Operations->>System: Create Cancellation record<br/>Cancellation date, reason, refund amount
            System->>System: Update Policy<br/>Status = CANCELLED

            alt Refund applicable
                System->>PaymentProcessor: Create refund request
                PaymentProcessor->>System: Confirm refund processed
                System->>System: Update Payment<br/>Status = REFUNDED
                System-->>Agent: Policy cancelled and refund completed
                Agent-->>Customer: Confirm cancellation and refund
            else No refund applicable
                System-->>Agent: Policy cancelled without refund
                Agent-->>Customer: Confirm cancellation
            end

        else Cancellation rejected
            Operations->>System: Reject cancellation request
            System-->>Agent: Cancellation rejected
            Agent-->>Customer: Inform cancellation rejection reason
        end
    end
    end

    %% 6. Natural Policy Expiry
    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over Customer,System: 6. Natural Policy Expiry

    opt Policy reaches end date without renewal
        System->>System: Check policy_end_date
        System->>System: Update Policy<br/>Status = EXPIRED
        System-->>Operations: Policy expired

        Operations->>System: Confirm expiry handling completed
        System-->>Agent: Notify policy expired
        Agent-->>Customer: Inform policy expired

        Note right of System: Natural expiry is system-driven when policy_end_date is reached.<br/>Operations may monitor expiry cases for reporting, renewal follow-up,<br/>or customer service handling.
    end
    end